      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Emma Lazarus’s translation, simply referred to as “Hymn” — derived from the piyyut יְיָ מָה אָדָם by Shlomo ibn Gabirol — was first published in her anthology, <tei:hi rend="italic">Songs of a Semite: The dance to death and other poems</tei:hi> (1882), pages 68-70. This is the first time we are aware of Emma Lazarus’s rhymed English translation being set side-by-side with ibn Gabirol’s Hebrew.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_62956_notes"/>
